# Exam track — Theme: Tourismus am Heemechtsland — Sub-lesson 3: Talking About It
# @question sentences: the examiner asks in Luxembourgish, the learner
# assembles the Luxembourgish answer (always en→lu).
#
# These are the user's real answers, gathered by interview on 2026-09-01
# (home country: Ukraine) — do not "improve" or genericize them in a later
# editing pass. The point is that the learner rehearses what they will
# actually say in the Sproochentest.
#
# Question texts come verbatim from the class handout, with two mechanical
# fixes: Festivaler -> Festivaller (LOD-flagged misspelling) and
# Sproochbarrièren fir -> Sproochbarrière fir (Eifeler Regel: -n drops
# before f).
#
# The @fill blocks carry frames that recur across any topic: well-causal,
# wann-conditional (x2), obwuel-contrast, comparative "léiwer wéi",
# "fir ... ze" purpose, fronted-adverb inversion (dofir), a duration blank,
# a frequency-adverb blank, and an "Ech mengen" hedge.

@lesson T1.03 "Talking About Tourism"

@word vu wou = where from
@word firwat = why
@word woufir = what for
@word de Westen = the west
@word de Krich = the war
@word sécher = safe
@word zimmlech = quite
@word d'Leit = the people
@word d'Sprooch = the language
@word schwätzen = to speak
@word de Kaffi = the coffee
@word d'Schlässer = the castles
@word d'Karpaten = the Carpathians
@word de Wuesstum = the growth
@word d'Wirtschaft = the economy
@word bekannt = well-known
@word onbekannt = unknown
@word den Nuetszuch = the night train
@word d'Flich = the flights
@word d'Regiounen = the regions
@word d'Zil = the destination
@word schmaachen = to taste
@word probéieren = to try
@word mengen = to think
@word d'Barrière = the barrier
@word manner = less
@word néierens = nowhere
@word heiansdo = sometimes
@word ëmmer = always
@word flott = nice

@sentence
@question Vu wou kommt Dir?
@lu Ech komme vun der Ukrain.
@en I come from Ukraine.
@distractor-lu wunnen
@distractor-lu Land
@distractor-en go
@distractor-en live

@sentence
@question Wéi ass d'Wieder an Ärem Heemechtsland?
@lu D'Wieder ass heiansdo extrem, de Wanter ass kal an de Summer ass waarm.
@en The weather is sometimes extreme, the winter is cold and the summer is warm.
@distractor-lu schéin
@distractor-lu frësch
@distractor-en beautiful
@distractor-en fresh

@sentence
@question Wéi ass d'Natur an Ärem Heemechtsland?
@lu Mir hu vill Bëscher an och d'Stepp.
@en We have many forests and also the steppe.
@distractor-lu Bierger
@distractor-lu Mier
@distractor-en mountains
@distractor-en sea

@sentence
@question Wéi eng Sprooche ginn an Ärem Heemechtsland geschwat?
@lu An der Ukrain schwätze mir Ukrainesch.
@en In Ukraine we speak Ukrainian.
@distractor-lu Englesch
@distractor-lu liesen
@distractor-en English
@distractor-en read

@sentence
@question Ginn et vill Touristen an Ärem Heemechtsland?
@lu Jo, am Weste vum Land gëtt et vill Touristen.
@en Yes, in the west of the country there are many tourists.
@distractor-lu Osten
@distractor-lu wéineg
@distractor-en east
@distractor-en few

@sentence
@question Ass Äert Heemechtsland touristefrëndlech? Firwat, firwat net?
@lu Jo, d'Land ass touristefrëndlech, well d'Leit ganz frëndlech sinn.
@en Yes, the country is tourist-friendly, because the people are very friendly.
@distractor-lu geféierlech
@distractor-lu ni
@distractor-en dangerous
@distractor-en never

@sentence
@question Ginn et geféierlech Plazen an Ärem Heemechtsland?
@lu Fréier war et méi geféierlech, mee virum Krich war et zimmlech sécher.
@en In the past it was more dangerous, but before the war it was quite safe.
@distractor-lu ëmmer
@distractor-lu wäit
@distractor-en always
@distractor-en far

@sentence
@question Wourop muss een als Tourist an Ärem Heemechtsland oppassen?
@lu Net op vill, well d'Land virum Krich sécher war.
@en Not much, because the country was safe before the war.
@distractor-lu alles
@distractor-lu Wieder
@distractor-en everything
@distractor-en weather

@sentence
@question Ginn et vill Touristenattraktiounen an Ärem Heemechtsland?
@lu Jo, virun allem an de grousse Stied an am Westen.
@en Yes, above all in the big cities and in the west.
@distractor-lu Dierfer
@distractor-lu keng
@distractor-en villages
@distractor-en none

@sentence
@question Wéi eng Aktivitéite kann een an Ärem Heemechtsland maachen?
@lu Ee ka wanderen an d'lokal Kichen entdecken.
@en One can hike and discover the local cuisine.
@distractor-lu schwammen
@distractor-lu kafen
@distractor-en swim
@distractor-en buy

@sentence
@question Wéi eng Saison ass am beschte fir Touristen an Ärem Heemechtsland?
@lu Déi bescht Saison ass de Summer.
@en The best season is the summer.
@distractor-lu Wanter
@distractor-lu deier
@distractor-en winter
@distractor-en expensive

@sentence
@question Wat sinn déi populärst Stied an Ärem Heemechtsland fir Touristen?
@lu Déi populärst Stied si Lwiw, Kiew, Charkiw an Odessa.
@en The most popular cities are Lviv, Kyiv, Kharkiv, and Odesa.
@distractor-lu Dierfer
@distractor-lu Bëscher
@distractor-en villages
@distractor-en forests

@sentence
@question Wat sollen Touristen an Ärem Heemechtsland besichen?
@lu Si sollen d'Schlässer am Weste vum Land besichtegen.
@en They should visit the castles in the west of the country.
@distractor-lu kafen
@distractor-lu Plagen
@distractor-en buy
@distractor-en beaches

@sentence
@question Woufir ass Äert Heemechtsland bekannt?
@lu D'Ukrain ass bekannt fir d'Iessen, fir Tschernobyl a fir al slawesch Monumenter.
@en Ukraine is known for the food, for Chernobyl, and for old Slavic landmarks.
@distractor-lu onbekannt
@distractor-lu Autoen
@distractor-en unknown
@distractor-en cars

@sentence
@question Wat sollen Touristen an Ärem Heemechtsland onbedéngt schmaachen?
@lu Si sollen onbedéngt Borschtsch, Varenyky an Holubtsi schmaachen.
@en They should definitely taste borsch, varenyky, and holubtsi.
@distractor-lu kachen
@distractor-lu kafen
@distractor-en cook
@distractor-en buy

@sentence
@question Hutt Dir schonn eng Kéier selwer Tourist an Ärem Heemechtsland gespillt?
@lu Jo, ech hunn déi meescht Regioune vun der Ukrain besichtegt.
@en Yes, I have visited most regions of Ukraine.
@distractor-lu keng
@distractor-lu verkaaft
@distractor-en none
@distractor-en sold

@sentence
@question Wéi verännert den Tourismus d'Wirtschaft an Ärem Heemechtsland?
@lu Den Tourismus ass net grouss, well d'Ukrain fir vill Leit onbekannt ass.
@en Tourism is not big, because Ukraine is unknown to many people.
@distractor-lu bekannt
@distractor-lu deier
@distractor-en famous
@distractor-en expensive

@sentence
@question Wat sinn déi bekanntste Festivaller oder Evenementer an Ärem Heemechtsland?
@lu Mir hu vill Festivaller mat Folklor a Musek.
@en We have many festivals with folklore and music.
@distractor-lu Muséeën
@distractor-lu deier
@distractor-en museums
@distractor-en expensive

@sentence
@question Wéi ass den Transport an Ärem Heemechtsland?
@lu Den Nuetszuch ass flott, mee de Bus ass manner gutt an d'Flich sinn deier.
@en The night train is nice, but the bus is less good and the flights are expensive.
@distractor-lu bëlleg
@distractor-lu Kaffi
@distractor-en cheap
@distractor-en coffee

@sentence
@question Wéi vill Hoteller oder Wunnenge sinn an Ärem Heemechtsland verfügbar fir Touristen?
@lu An den touristesche Regioune sinn d'Hoteller gutt.
@en In the tourist regions the hotels are good.
@distractor-lu schlecht
@distractor-lu Muséeën
@distractor-en bad
@distractor-en museums

@sentence
@question Ginn et vill Muséeën an Ärem Heemechtsland?
@lu Jo, mee si sinn net sou modern wéi an Europa.
@en Yes, but they are not as modern as in Europe.
@distractor-lu deier
@distractor-lu ni
@distractor-en expensive
@distractor-en never

@sentence
@question Ginn et Plazen, déi méi wéineg besicht ginn, mee interessant fir Touriste sinn?
@lu Jo, d'Schlässer am Weste vum Land si manner bekannt, mee ganz interessant.
@en Yes, the castles in the west of the country are less known, but very interesting.
@distractor-lu Plagen
@distractor-lu deier
@distractor-en beaches
@distractor-en expensive

@sentence
@question Wat denkt Dir iwwert de Wuesstum vum Tourismus an Ärem Heemechtsland?
@lu De Wuesstum ass nach kleng, well vill Leit d'Ukrain net kennen.
@en The growth is still small, because many people don't know Ukraine.
@distractor-lu grouss
@distractor-lu deier
@distractor-en big
@distractor-en expensive

@sentence
@question Gëtt et Sproochbarrière fir Touristen, déi Äert Heemechtsland besichen?
@lu D'Sprooch kann eng Barrière sinn, mee et gëtt ëmmer besser.
@en The language can be a barrier, but it is getting better.
@distractor-lu Kichen
@distractor-lu ni
@distractor-en cuisine
@distractor-en never

@sentence
@question Wéi kënnen Touristen eng richteg Erfarung mat der lokaler Kultur maachen?
@lu D'Leit si frëndlech a weisen den Touriste gär hir Kultur.
@en The people are friendly and gladly show the tourists their culture.
@distractor-lu verkafen
@distractor-lu ni
@distractor-en sell
@distractor-en never

@sentence
@question Wat fir Rotschléi hutt Dir fir Touristen, déi fir déi éischt Kéier an Äert Heemechtsland reesen?
@lu Probéiert de Kaffi zu Kiew an zu Lwiw, well en néierens sou gutt ass.
@en Try the coffee in Kyiv and in Lviv, because it is nowhere as good.
@distractor-lu Zopp
@distractor-lu deier
@distractor-en soup
@distractor-en expensive

